<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3929" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăsĭnīnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		asinus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>produced by an ass</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stercus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 38, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pullus,</span>”
				<i>ass's foal</i>, <i>a young ass</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 2, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pilus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 21, 30, § 72</span></i>
			, where Jan reads <i>asini</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pruna asinina cognominata a vilitate,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					15, 13, 12, § 41</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
